# Redis

A Redis-inspired in-memory key-value server written in C++.

## Features

* TCP client-server communication
* In-memory key-value storage
* Key expiration (TTL)
* Sorted sets
* Custom hash table
* AVL tree and heap implementations
* Thread pool for background tasks

## Build

```bash
g++ -std=c++11 -pthread \
    server.cpp hashtable.cpp avl.cpp heap.cpp \
    zset.cpp thread_pool.cpp \
    -o redis_server
```

## Run

```bash
./redis_server
```

Connect using the included client or a TCP client such as `netcat`:

```bash
nc localhost <port>
```

## Structure

```text
server.cpp          Server and networking
client.cpp          Client
hashtable.cpp       Key-value storage
avl.cpp             AVL tree
zset.cpp            Sorted sets
heap.cpp            TTL management
thread_pool.cpp     Worker thread pool
```
